+++### Step-by-Step Guide: Authoring & Requesting Dual-Control Custom Scripted Fields
+++
+++1. **Navigate to Custom Fields Studio:** Open `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/custom-fields` and click **`New Custom Field`**.
+++2. **Configure Baseline Attributes:**
+++   - Set **Display Name** (e.g. `Cross-Project Security Compliance Score`).
+++   - Define **Field Slug** (`cross-proj-sec-score`).
+++   - Select **Flavor / Tier** (e.g. `formula` or `wasm`).
+++   - Set **Output Format** to `severity_pill` or `number`.
+++3. **Select Elevated Scope / Service Account:**
+++   - In the **Target Scope Tier** dropdown, select `WORKSPACE` or `SERVER`.
+++   - Optionally toggle **Credential Mode** to `SERVICE_ACCOUNT` if the script must run under service authority.
+++   - The UI immediately renders an amber unmissable **Dual-Control Escalation Banner** warning of the expanded tenant blast radius.
+++4. **Draft and Test Execute:**
+++   - Author your formula expression or compiled module.
+++   - Click **`Test Execute`** to verify execution in memory against sample payloads.
+++5. **Submit Escalation Request:**
+++   - Click **`Save & Request Escalation`**.
+++   - An escalation proposal is created and dispatched to the approval queue with pending status.
+++6. **Independent Admin Review & Cryptographic Approval:**
