"monospace\": true\n}\n```\n\n### 2. `number`\nFloating point or integer numeric value with precision limits, suffix, and range bounds.\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"number\",\n  \"maximum_fraction_digits\": 2,\n  \"unit_suffix\": \" hrs\",\n  \"min_value\": 0.0,\n  \"max_value\": 1000.0\n}\n```\n\n### 3. `badge`\nVisual status badge with color token and strict label allowlist. Supported color tokens: `neutral`, `info`, `success`, `warning`, `danger`, `accent`.\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"badge\",\n  \"color_token\": \"success\",\n  \"allowed_labels\": [\"Passed\", \"Failed\", \"In Progress\", \"Pending\"]\n}\n```\n\n### 4. `severity_pill`\nStandardized vulnerability and risk assessment pill. Accepts a dictionary with a required `\"level\"` (`\"low\"`, `\"medium\"`, `\"high\"`, `\"critical\"`), and optional numeric `\"score\"` (finite float between `0.0` and `10.0`) and optional `\"label\"` (string of at most 32 characters without HTML markup).\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"severity_pill\"\n}\n```\n\n### 5. `url`\nSanitized hyperlink validated against allowed schemes and host suffixes.\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"url\",\n  \"allowed_schemes\": [\"https\"],\n  \"allowed_host_suffixes\": [\"github.com\", \"gitlab.com\"]\n}\n```\n\n### 6. `markdown_snippet`\nSanitized canonical Markdown snippet rendered inline up to 2000 characters.\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"markdown_snippet\",\n  \"max_chars\": 2000\n}\n```\n\n### 7. `json_table`\nStructured 2-dimensional tabular data rendered directly in the issue details view.\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"json_table\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\"key\": \"test_name\", \"label\": \"Test Suite\"},\n    {\"key\": \"duration_ms\", \"label\": \"Duration (ms)\"},\n    {\"key\": \"status\", \"label\": \"Status\"}\n  ],\n  \"max_rows\": 25\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Safe Formula Context Reference\n\nWhen writing Safe Formulas, expressions have access to the active issue attributes without executing arbitrary code:\n\n| Variable | Type | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `id` | `str` | Issue unique identifier (UUID) |\n| `key` | `str` | Human-readable issue key (e.g. `KAN-32`) |\n| `summary` | `str` | Issue title / summary |\n| `description_markdown` | `str` | Raw Markdown body of the issue |\n| `state` | `str` | Name of current workflow state (e.g. `In Progress`) |\n| `state_group` | `str` | Workflow state category (`backlog`, `unstarted`, `started`, `completed`, `cancelled`) |\n| `priority` | `str` | Normalized uppercase priority (`URGENT`, `HIGH`, `MEDIUM`, `LOW`, `NONE`) |\n| `priority_slug` | `str` | Lowercase priority slug (`urgent`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `none`) |\n| `priority_label` | `str` | Display label of priority (`Urgent`, `High`, etc.) |\n| `start_date` | `str` or `None` | ISO-formatted start date |\n| `due_date` | `str` or `None` | ISO-formatted due date |\n| `days_until_due` | `int` or `None` | Days until due date (negative values indicate overdue) |\n| `blocker_count` | `int` | Number of active blocking dependencies on this issue |\n| `sub_issue_count` | `int` | Total count of child sub-issues |\n| `completed_sub_issue_count`| `int` | Count of sub-issues in `completed` state group |\n| `labels` | `list[str]` | List of tag names assigned to the issue |\n\n### Safe Built-in Functions\nSafe formulas allow standard deterministic operations: `round`, `int`, `float`, `min`, `max`, `len`, `abs`, `str`. Arbitrary imports, file system access, and network sockets are strictly prohibited at the Python AST parser layer.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testing, Dry-Running, and Scope Escalation\n\n### Dry-Running with Test Execute\nBefore saving any custom field definition, use the **Test Execute** button in the Custom Field Definition Editor or send a POST request to:\n```http\nPOST /api/v1/projects/{project_ref}/custom-fields/test-execute\n```\nThis evaluates your formula or script against a mock issue payload or existing issue key in memory without persisting values or polluting the audit ledger. In Standalone mode, Test Execute verifies that your script does not request unavailable sandbox tiers.\n\n### Scope Escalation and AAL2 Dual-Control Approval\nCustom fields can be scoped at three tiers:\n- **`PROJECT` Scope:** Can only read and affect issues within the parent project. Requires Project Administrator privileges.\n- **`WORKSPACE` Scope:** Can read issues across all projects in the workspace.\n- **`SERVER` Scope:** Global fields available across all workspaces.\n\n![Custom Fields Dual Control Escalation](images/slice5-custom-fields-escalation-dual-control-desktop-1440x900-light.png)\n\n**Dual-Control Governance:** Escalating a custom field definition from `PROJECT` to `WORKSPACE` or `SERVER` scope (or running with elevated Service Account credentials rather than `INVOKING_USER`) requires cryptographic approval by an administrator of that target tier with active Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2 / WebAuthn / TOTP) session elevation.\n\n### Step-by-Step Guide: Authoring & Requesting Dual-Control Custom Scripted Fields\n\n1. **Navigate to Custom Fields Studio:** Open `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/custom-fields` and click **`New Custom Field`**.\n2. **Configure Baseline Attributes:**\n   - Set **Display Name** (e.g. `Cross-Project Security Compliance Score`).\n   - Define **Field Slug** (`cross-proj-sec-score`).\n   - Select **Flavor / Tier** (e.g. `formula` or `wasm`).\n   - Set **Output Format** to `severity_pill` or `number`.\n3. **Select Elevated Scope / Service Account:**\n   - In the **Target Scope Tier** dropdown, select `WORKSPACE` or `SERVER`.\n   - Optionally toggle **Credential Mode** to `SERVICE_ACCOUNT` if the script must run under service authority.\n   - The UI immediately renders an amber unmissable **Dual-Control Escalation Banner** warning of the expanded tenant blast radius.\n4. **Draft and Test Execute:**\n   - Author your formula expression or compiled module.\n   - Click **`Test Execute`** to verify execution in memory against sample payloads.\n5. **Submit Escalation Request:**\n   - Click **`Save & Request Escalation`**.\n   - An escalation proposal is created and dispatched to the approval queue with pending status.\n6. **Independent Admin Review & Cryptographic Approval:**\n   - A distinct Workspace or Server Administrator opens `/projects/<PROJECT_KEY>/settings/custom-fields` (or the Escalation Approvals panel).\n   - The reviewer inspects script source, requested scope, credential mode, and blast radius.\n   - The reviewer clicks **`Approve Escalation`** and provides fresh Authenticator Assurance Level 2 (AAL2) credentials (biometric Passkey, hardware FIDO2 key, or 6-digit TOTP code).\n   - Upon AAL2 verification, the approval is cryptographically sealed, logged in the activity ledger, and the escalated custom field activates immediately.\n\n---\n\n## Custom Field Configuration Attributes and Controls\n\n### Display Name\nThe human-readable title of the custom field shown on ticket property rails, board cards, and table columns.\n\n### Slug\nThe unique, URL-safe ASCII identifier used in formulas, API payloads, and query filters.\n\n### Flavors\nDetermines the underlying calculation mechanism: `scalar`, `formula`, `wasm`, or `nsjail`.\n\n### Sandbox Tier\nSelects between in-process WebAssembly (`wasmtime` Tier A) and containerized Linux namespaces (`nsjail` Tier B). In Standalone mode, `nsjail` is gated.\n\n### Credential Mode\nSpecifies whether the field executes with `INVOKING_USER` permissions or elevated `SERVICE_ACCOUNT` credentials.\n\n### Target Scope\nControls the tenant boundary accessible to the custom field: `PROJECT`, `WORKSPACE`, or `SERVER`.\n\n### Output Formats\nCanonical schema used to format and validate the output: `text`, `number`, `badge`, `severity_pill`, `url`, `markdown_snippet`, or `json_table`.\n\n### Format Metadata\nJSON metadata configuring format-specific options such as decimal precision, color tokens, and table column schemas.\n\n### Script Source\nThe Python AST expression, compiled WebAssembly module, or sandboxed script implementing the field calculation.\n\n### Egress Allowlist\nExplicit list of destination hosts accessible to `nsjail` tier scripts. Network access is disabled by default via `CLONE_NEWNET`.\n\n### AAL2 Stepup\nAdministrative modifications and scope escalations require recent multi-factor authentication (AAL2 verified within 900 seconds).\n\n### Approvals\nEscalating a field to workspace or server scope requires explicit cryptographic signing and approval by an administrator of that target tier.\n"
