ard authentication, air-gap flags, and cryptographic permanent purge.\n7. **Scoped MCP Agent (Service Principal):** Autonomous or assisted agent accessing `/mcp/agent`, `/mcp/docs`, or `/mcp/admin` bound to an API key or OAuth 2.0 PKCE token.\n\n---\n\n## Workspace-Level Roles\n\n### Master Capability Matrix\n\n| Operational Capability | Guest | Viewer | Member | Project Admin | Workspace Admin | Server Admin | Scoped MCP Agent |\n| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Viewing Workspace-Public Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Viewing Private Project Objects** | \u25d0 (2) | \u25d0 (2) | \u25d0 (2) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 2) |\n| **Explicit ACL DENY Precedence** | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) | \u25cf (3) |\n| **Authoring Issues, Stickies, and Docs** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Editing and Versioning Pages** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Managing Resource ACLs (Share / Revoke)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (4) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 4) |\n| **Project Studio and Workflow Management** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Custom Field and Script Definition** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (5) | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 5) |\n| **Soft-Trash Project Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (6) | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25cf | \u25d0 (1, 6) |\n| **Workspace Trash Studio Inspection** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (7) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1, 8) |\n| **Restoring Soft-Deleted Objects** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (7) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1, 8) |\n| **Workspace Retention Policy (7 to 365 Days)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Automated Multi-Object Sweep (trash_purge)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (9) | \u25cb |\n| **2-Stage Permanent Purge (Cryptographic)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8, 10) | \u25cb |\n| **Local User Provisioning and Password Reset** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Role Bindings and Group Hierarchy CRUD** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25d0 (11) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Multi-Card Auth Studio and Passkey Config** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Minting Scoped MCP API Keys** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25cb |\n| **Immutable Audit Ledger (Inspection Only)** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cf (8) | \u25cf (8) | \u25d0 (1) |\n| **Tampering with Audit Ledger Records** | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb | \u25cb (12) | \u25cb |\n\n---\n\n## Detailed Condition Notes\n\n1. **Token Scope Restriction:** Scoped MCP Agents can only exercise capabilities explicitly included in their minted token scopes (`read:issues`, `write:issues`, `read:docs`, `write:docs`, `admin`, etc.). Unscoped tools are rejected with `403 FORBIDDEN`.\n2. **Explicit Project Membership / ACL Share:** Guests and Viewers cannot see private project entities unless explicitly added to the project role bindings or granted a specific `ALLOW` entry in `resource_acl_entries`.\n3. **Absolute DENY Precedence:** If an explicit `DENY` entry exists for a principal on an object (or inherited group), effective capability bitmasks collapse immediately (`allow & (~deny)`). Even Workspace Admins cannot view or manage objects guarded by an explicit `DENY`.\n4. **Ownership Share Delegation:** Standard Members can only share objects they originally authored, provided project policy permits user-level ACL delegation.\n5. **Admin Approval Gate:** Custom fields and scripts can only be defined by administrators. Executing a script with Workspace or Server token escalation requires cryptographic approval from an administrator of that tier.\n6. **Author Deletion Scope:** Members may soft-delete their own drafts, comments, and un-assigned stickies if granted DELETE capability mask. Project-wide item soft-deletion requires Project Admin.\n7. **Project Scope Isolation:** Project Admins in the Trash Studio can only view and restore items belonging to projects where they hold explicit `PROJECT_ADMIN` authority.\n8. **Fresh AAL2 Step-Up Requirement:** All administrative endpoints (`/api/v1/admin/*`, retention settings, user provisioning, trash operations, key minting) enforce `Depends(require_admin_aal2)`. The session must have verified MFA within the last 900 seconds (`aal2_verified_at <= 900s`).\n9. **Daemon Background Job Authority:** The trash purge runner executes with dedicated system worker identity and sweeps expired entities strictly past their per-workspace `trash_retention_days` threshold.\n10. **2-Stage Destructive Confirmation:** Permanent purge is exclusively gated to `SERVER_ADMIN` + fresh AAL2. It requires `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:request` to compute blast radius and mint an ephemeral HMAC `confirmation_token` + `blast_hash`, followed by `POST /api/v1/admin/destructive:execute` with a mandatory human reason (10 to 500 characters).\n11. **Project-Level Role Delegation:** Project Admins may manage role bindings within their designated project only. They cannot elevate users to Workspace Admin or Server Admin.\n12. **Cryptographic Immutability:** Audit ledger tables (`activity_ledger`) have no `UPDATE` or `DELETE` grants for any database role (including `kanban_app` and `kanban_migrator`). Triggers prevent tampering.\n\n---\n\n## Architectural Security Invariants\n\n- **Hostile Wire Invariant:** Every input is validated with strict Pydantic schemas and UTF-8 surrogate checks. Cleartext transmission of tokens is prohibited.\n- **Walled Component Garden:** Row-Level Security (`FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`) is always active on all database sessions. Dropp